# Integration Best Practices

## Slack

- Webhook does NOT support channel override. Use Bot Token API (`chat.postMessage`) for dynamic channels
- Buttons in `actions` blocks require Interactivity URL. Use mrkdwn links in `context` blocks instead
- Channel names reject underscores. Sanitize: `sdr_v3` → `sdr-v3` via `.replace('_', '-')`
- Bot must be `/invite`d to each channel before posting

## Supabase / Database

- GENERATED columns reject INSERT. Omit them from payloads (e.g. computed scores)
- Know the schema before inserting — validate column names against the actual table, never assume
- `.in()` does NOT accept query builders as subqueries — always pass a plain array

## LLM Evaluation (G-Eval)

- Client silence != dissatisfaction. Instruct model: "assume neutral 5-6 if no explicit feedback"
- Few-shot anchors must come from real production data, not invented examples
- LLM scores dimensions; Python computes weighted overall score. Never let the LLM assign the final score

## URLs and External References

- Validate URLs against the real system before hardcoding
- SSM naming: `/{service}-{stage}-{param}`. Copy pattern from existing parameters

## Tests

- If test describes correct UX behavior, fix the code (e.g. message splitter merge logic)
- If production code evolved legitimately, fix the test assertion
- Mocks must support the full query API chain (e.g. `.not_.is_()` for Supabase filters)

## Deploy

- Local changes do NOT affect Lambda. Redeploy before validating any change
- All messages visible to users must be in PT-BR
